    "method": "Three writers/researchers cross-reviewed different branches. Parent applied and integrated corrections; reviewers rechecked the substantive fixes.",
    "scope": "Selected mathematical statements, proofs, prerequisites and cited-theorem hypotheses. This is not verification of every external research proof.",
    "findings": [
      {
        "note": "4P0M",
        "reviewer": "Faraday",
        "issue": "Pure log(1/delta) noise bound cannot hold up to delta approaching one.",
        "resolution": "Restricted to 0<delta<=1/2; constants and sample threshold enlarged. Author-version appendices A and J and Lemma 6 checked for confidence allocation.",
        "status": "resolved"
      },
      {
        "note": "4P0R",
        "reviewer": "Faraday",
        "issue": "Binary label domain was implicit.",
        "resolution": "Added y in {-1,1}.",
        "status": "resolved"
      },
      {
        "note": "4Q0T",
        "reviewer": "Boyle",
        "issue": "Conditional drift needs uniform conditional failure probabilities given each block-start history.",
        "resolution": "Added explicit stronger history-conditional regret hypothesis and empty initial state; c_delta and q give drift [-(1-q)c_delta+qn]T<0. Source lemmas and moment theorem remain cited inputs.",
        "status": "resolved"
      },
      {
        "note": "4R0G",
        "reviewer": "Gibbs",
        "issue": "Wording unnecessarily limited Newton equations to the central path.",
        "resolution": "Stated strict primal/dual feasibility without equal coordinate products.",
        "status": "resolved"
      },
      {
        "note": "4R0I",
        "reviewer": "Gibbs",
        "issue": "Feasible steps alone do not ensure the central-neighborhood estimate on later iterations.",
        "resolution": "Required every accepted step to stay in N_gamma.",
        "status": "resolved"
      },
      {
        "note": "4R0K",
        "reviewer": "Gibbs",
        "issue": "Convergence context needed a saddle-existence hypothesis; cited section discusses ergodic averages.",
        "resolution": "Added saddle existence, defined arithmetic averages and aligned attribution with the report's ergodic discussion; local proof covers fixed-point optimality.",
        "status": "resolved"
      },
      {
        "notes": [
          "4R0G",
          "4R0H",
          "4R0W",
          "4R10"
        ],
        "reviewer": "Gibbs and parent",
        "issue": "A few source equation/section labels were stale or incorrect.",
        "resolution": "Checked against publisher HTML and regenerated manifest.",
        "status": "resolved"
      }
    ],
